From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:21:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ofono: an ended incoming call is disconnected, not incoming

OfonoVoiceCallHandler::status() reported a call that had been through the
incoming call filter with ACTION_CONTINUE as STATUS_INCOMING for oFono's
"disconnected" state as well as for "incoming". The "disconnected" case is
there so that a filtered call can still be told apart as rejected or
ignored once it has gone, but for a call the filter let through it made
every answered incoming call report itself as incoming again at the moment
it ended.

A client that opens its incoming call UI on STATUS_INCOMING - the LuneOS
phone app does - then showed a fresh incoming call screen for a call that
had just been hung up, and the MCE plugin briefly announced "ringing" for
it as well.

Report STATUS_DISCONNECTED for a let-through call that has disconnected;
rejected and ignored calls keep reporting as before.

Seen with oFono phonesim on a Zinwa Q25: voicecall logged
"STATE: ringing" between "active" and "none" on every hang-up, and the
phone app put up the incoming call page again.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending [written against 8e6ec88, intended for sailfishos/voicecall]
---
 plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.cpp b/plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.cpp
index 2db69a5..b974dc7 100644
--- a/plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.cpp
+++ b/plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.cpp
@@ -195,7 +195,11 @@ AbstractVoiceCallHandler::VoiceCallStatus OfonoVoiceCallHandler::status() const
     } else if (d->filterHasRun && (state == "incoming" || state == "disconnected")) {
         switch (d->filterAction) {
         case ACTION_CONTINUE:
-            return STATUS_INCOMING;
+            /* Only a call still ringing is incoming. Once one that was let
+             * through has ended it is disconnected like any other: reporting
+             * it as incoming again made every answered call look like a new
+             * incoming call for the moment it took to go away. */
+            return state == "disconnected" ? STATUS_DISCONNECTED : STATUS_INCOMING;
         case ACTION_IGNORE:
             return STATUS_IGNORED;
         case ACTION_REJECT:
